{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115756",
      "title": "A Closer Look at Decorator-based Queries & Lifecycle Hooks",
      "lectureOrder": 135,
      "videoOrder": 129,
      "sourceHash": "124c53dc4eb81b5e3c9bbfa7b6e2eb9705f2d62b3ff56ccc21a9dead2e48af14",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "Now that we covered view child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "and Content Child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "we can also explore some new lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 11.22,
          "en": "that are worth mentioning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.22,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "Now it's the after view and after content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 18.24,
          "en": "Init lifecycle hooks I want to take a closer look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.24,
          "end": 21.13,
          "en": "before we then also explore after next render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.016,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "and after render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "Because these hooks can be useful if you are dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 29.58,
          "en": "with elements that have been selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.58,
          "end": 33.39,
          "en": "with help of view child or content child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.39,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "And therefore let's start with the after view Init hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 41.246,
          "en": "To avoid typos, I'll again implement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.246,
          "end": 46.246,
          "en": "the after view Init interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 49.29,
          "en": "that is provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 52.36,
          "en": "and that is imported from at Angular core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "because this interface then forces me to implement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 60.633,
          "en": "the NG after view Init method like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 64.65,
          "en": "You can also omit this colon white thing here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "that just tells TypeScript that this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 69.813,
          "en": "doesn't need to return anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 75.89,
          "en": "But here I can then log after view Init",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.9,
          "end": 79.533,
          "en": "and what's now the idea behind this hook?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 84.87,
          "en": "Well, in this hook here, you are guaranteed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.87,
          "end": 87.42,
          "en": "to have access to the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.42,
          "end": 90.163,
          "en": "that have been selected with view child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.163,
          "end": 93.45,
          "en": "unless you of course specified some selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.45,
          "end": 95.19,
          "en": "that can't be found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.19,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "But you are guaranteed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 99.03,
          "en": "that the template has been initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.03,
          "end": 100.95,
          "en": "and that in theory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.95,
          "end": 105.12,
          "en": "Angular therefore is able to select elements in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.12,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "So here we can cons log this forum native element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 111.60300000000001,
          "en": "and we should get a result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.92,
          "end": 117.09,
          "en": "On the other hand, if I also implement on Init,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.09,
          "end": 119.1,
          "en": "so this on Init interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.1,
          "end": 122.263,
          "en": "which is also imported from Angular core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.263,
          "end": 127.05,
          "en": "and I therefore add the NG on Init method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.05,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "which you already saw before earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 133.44,
          "en": "I'm not guaranteed that this element exists yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.44,
          "end": 135.43,
          "en": "So if I log on Init here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "and I try to access the native element here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 142.8,
          "en": "you'll see that if I actually go away from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.8,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "that signal form here, back to using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.74,
          "end": 147.75,
          "en": "that view chart decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.75,
          "end": 150.333,
          "en": "and therefore I'm not executing this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.333,
          "end": 153.67000000000002,
          "en": "but instead I'm accessing the native element like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.01,
          "end": 159.93,
          "en": "and also like that down here, if I change that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 164.04,
          "en": "and I save it all, you'll see that now if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.04,
          "end": 167.04,
          "en": "I got the on Init log here, this one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.04,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "but then I see undefined for that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 173.46,
          "en": "that I'm trying to get hold of with view child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.46,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "Whereas in after view Init, I do get hold of that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 179.673,
          "en": "That's the difference here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.11,
          "end": 183.18,
          "en": "Now things are a little bit different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.18,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "if you're using the view child function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 188.07,
          "en": "There, you can actually also read it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 189.66,
          "en": "inside of Init.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.66,
          "end": 191.25,
          "en": "But when using that decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.25,
          "end": 193.95,
          "en": "there is this important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.95,
          "end": 195.647,
          "en": "which you should be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.647,
          "end": 199.07999999999998,
          "en": "because that difference of course means that if you're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 201.69,
          "en": "that decorator for selecting an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.69,
          "end": 203.52,
          "en": "and storing it in a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.52,
          "end": 206.348,
          "en": "and you then wanna do something with that element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.348,
          "end": 209.338,
          "en": "you can only do so in after view Init",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.338,
          "end": 213.51,
          "en": "or any of your methods that are triggered from the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.51,
          "end": 215.67000000000002,
          "en": "but not inside of NgOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.67000000000002,
          "end": 218.49,
          "en": "because there it would still be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.49,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "That's something to be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 222.28,
          "en": "and something to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.414,
          "end": 225.93,
          "en": "and that's why this lifecycle hook exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.93,
          "end": 229.11,
          "en": "And that's also why we have this NG",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.11,
          "end": 232.29,
          "en": "after content Init lifecycle hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 234.39,
          "en": "because here in the control component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 239.39,
          "en": "if I implement after content Init,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.43,
          "end": 243.42,
          "en": "which of course also is imported from at Angular core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.42,
          "end": 245.787,
          "en": "and I therefore then add the NG",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.96,
          "end": 251.61,
          "en": "after content in IT method here, I can safely access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.61,
          "end": 256.44,
          "en": "that content assuming that I got a correct selector here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.44,
          "end": 258.99,
          "en": "inside of NG after content Init,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258.99,
          "end": 262.23,
          "en": "no matter if I'm using the content child function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.23,
          "end": 267.23,
          "en": "or the content child decorator, just as with at view child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.72,
          "end": 271.26,
          "en": "at content child would not produce a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.26,
          "end": 274.803,
          "en": "if I would try to access it inside of on Init,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.7,
          "end": 279.06,
          "en": "inside of NG after content Init on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "I'm guaranteed to get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 283.68,
          "en": "of these values that are selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.68,
          "end": 287.64,
          "en": "with the content child selector if I did specify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.64,
          "end": 289.623,
          "en": "a valid selector here, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.88,
          "end": 294.043,
          "en": "So that's the idea behind NG after content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.043,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "Init and NG after view Init.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
